<div style="font-family: monospace; padding: 24px; max-width: 760px; line-height: 1.6;">
  <h2 style="margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 18px;">
    Privacy Policy
    <a href={~p"/"} class="gh-link">← back to the ray tracer</a>
  </h2>

  <p style="font-size: 12px; color: #888; margin-bottom: 24px;">
    Last updated: 7 September 2026
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">1. What this site is</h3>
  <p>
    This site renders a ray traced image in your browser. There are no accounts, no logins
    and no file uploads. The settings you choose (canvas size, sphere radius, colours, eye
    and light positions) are held in memory for the duration of your visit and are discarded
    when you close the page. Nothing you render is stored on the server.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">2. Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    This site uses <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GoatCounter</a>,
    a privacy friendly analytics service, to get a rough idea of how many people visit.
    GoatCounter sets no cookies, does not track you across websites and does not build a
    profile of you. For each page view it records: the page address, the referring page (if
    any), your browser and operating system, your screen size and your country. Your IP
    address is used only to work out the country and to tell one visit from another within a
    single day; it is not stored.
  </p>
  <p style="margin-top: 8px;">
    The details are described in the
    <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GoatCounter privacy policy</a>
    and <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/gdpr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GDPR notes</a>.
    If you would rather not be counted, block the domain <code>gc.zgo.at</code> in your
    browser or content blocker, or run
    <code>localStorage.setItem('skipgc', 't')</code> in your browser console once for this site.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">3. Cookies</h3>
  <p>
    One strictly necessary cookie is set (<code>_ray_tracer_web_key</code>). It holds a signed
    session token used to protect the page against cross site request forgery. It contains no
    personal data, is not used for analytics or advertising and expires when your browser
    session ends.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">4. Rate limiting</h3>
  <p>
    The number of renders a single visitor can request is limited, so that the server stays
    usable for everyone. To enforce that, your IP address is held briefly in the server's
    memory along with a counter. It is not written to a database, it is discarded once the
    counter expires and it is not shared with anyone.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">5. Server logs</h3>
  <p>
    The hosting provider records ordinary web server logs (IP address, timestamp, requested
    page, browser identification) for security and troubleshooting. These are kept only as
    long as the provider needs them for those purposes.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">6. Your rights</h3>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct or erase personal data concerning
    you, to restrict or object to its processing, and to lodge a complaint with your data
    protection authority. Since this site keeps no accounts and stores no identifiable
    records, there is normally nothing to retrieve or delete, but you are welcome to ask.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">7. Contact</h3>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or about how data is handled here:
    <a href="mailto:privacy@codingful.com">privacy@codingful.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 24px 0 8px;">8. Changes</h3>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page will be updated. There is no
    mailing list, so please check back here if it matters to you.
  </p>
</div>
